# ig-wrapped

## Stack

- **Backend:** Node.js (ESM), Express 4, Multer, CORS.
- **Frontend:** React 18, Vite 5.
- **Language:** JavaScript only (no TypeScript in this repo).

## Run (local)

- **Backend:** `cd backend` → `npm install` → `npm run dev` → `http://localhost:4000`
- **Frontend:** `cd frontend` → `npm install` → `npm run dev` → `http://localhost:5173`

## Hosting

- **Frontend:** Vercel — static Vite build. Root directory **`frontend`**, framework preset Vite, output `dist`.
- **Backend:** Render Web Service — Root directory **`backend`**, start command `npm start`, listens on `process.env.PORT || 4000`.
- **`VITE_API_URL`** env var (set in Vercel dashboard, Production + Preview) gives the frontend the backend upload URL. Baked in at **build time** — redeploy frontend after changing it.
- **`frontend/vercel.json`** — SPA catch-all rewrite so deep links to `/heatmap`, `/social-graph`, `/wrapped`, etc. work on refresh.
- **`.github/workflows/frontend-ci.yml`** — runs `npm ci && npm run build` on PRs touching `frontend/**`.

## Folder map

- **`backend/src/`** — `server.js`, `app.js`; **`routes/upload.js`** (multipart upload); **`services/compareUsers.js`**; **`parsers/instagramParsers.js`**; **`middleware/errorHandler.js`**
- **`frontend/src/`** — **`App.jsx`** (routes: `/`, `/heatmap`, `/social-graph`, `/messages`, `/most-used-words`, `/wrapped`); **`pages/`** (feature pages); **`utils/`** — `commentHeatmap.js`, `socialInteractionGraph.js`, `messageFrequency.js`, `mostUsedWords.js`, `wrappedData.js`, `profileSearches.js`; **`styles.css`**
- **`frontend/.env.example`** — documents `VITE_API_URL`
- **`frontend/vercel.json`** — SPA rewrite rule

## API

- **`POST /upload`** (`multipart/form-data`): `followersFile`, `followingFile` (Instagram export JSON) → JSON `{ "non_followers": ["user1", ...] }`
- **`GET /health`** → `{ "ok": true }`
- Upload URL in frontend: `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL ?? "http://localhost:4000/upload"`

## Conventions

- Match existing style: focused diffs, no unrelated refactors.
- **Non-Followers** flow uses the backend API; **Activity Heatmap**, **Social Graph**, **Messages**, **Most used words**, and **Wrapped** parse export data **entirely in the browser** (folder picker, no extra chart libraries beyond what the app already uses). **Wrapped** (`/wrapped`) is a client-only swipeable recap (activity + three social leaderboards + DMs + searches + privacy) once the export folder is loaded in context.
- When adding Instagram export parsing, reuse patterns from **`frontend/src/utils/commentHeatmap.js`** and align with **`socialInteractionGraph.js`** where overlap exists.

## Optional scoped rules

Add separate `.mdc` files with `globs` (e.g. `frontend/**/*.jsx`, `backend/**/*.js`) if you need frontend-only or backend-only guidance beyond this file.
